  <h2 id="headroom">Where the top pay comes from: headroom, ownership and AI</h2>

  <p>
    High pay after 12th mostly comes from one of four moves: scarce skill, revenue ownership, regulation or
    scale. A salary band alone rarely gets a person to the top of any of these professions.
  </p>

  <div class="work-style-grid">
    <div class="work-style-card">
      <div class="work-style-card__label">Software and data</div>
      <div class="work-style-card__title">Scale through shipped work</div>
      <p>The median moves when you can show a deployed project, a data dashboard or an automated workflow. AI now writes first drafts of routine code, so the human layer is design, checking and explaining trade-offs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="work-style-card">
      <div class="work-style-card__label">CA, audit and finance</div>
      <div class="work-style-card__title">Scale through advisory and ownership</div>
      <p>Compliance work pays a salary. Advisory clients, a small practice or a niche such as GST or startup accounting let you own pricing. AI speeds reconciliation, but review and signature stay human.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="work-style-card">
      <div class="work-style-card__label">Law</div>
      <div class="work-style-card__title">Scale through a practice or a niche</div>
      <p>Contracts, compliance and disputes can be built into your own practice with repeat clients. Research and drafting are where AI compresses junior work first.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="work-style-card">
      <div class="work-style-card__label">Health and pharmacy</div>
      <div class="work-style-card__title">Scale through specialisation</div>
      <p>Specialist doctors, pharmacy owners and independent diagnostic or consulting services scale beyond a fixed band. Licensing and supervised practice cannot be self-taught or skipped.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>The ownership path:</strong> a CA practice, a law practice, a pharmacy, a software product or
      a design studio each let you own pricing and repeat clients. That is why a fixed pay band is a starting
      layer rather than a ceiling for these paths.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    Start using AI now as a study and checking partner: ask it to explain a concept, then verify the answer
    from a textbook or official page, and never submit an unchecked number. Later, as tools and adoption
    mature, the leverage grows for people who pair deep domain knowledge with a clear workflow and can show
    the result. No multiplier is guaranteed, and tool skills without domain depth do not raise pay.
  </p>

